Traversal + Counting Pattern.

public class Solution {
    public static int countEvenNumbers(int[] arr, int n) {
        // Write your code here
        int count=0;
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            if(arr[i] % 2==0){
                count++;
            }
        }
        return count;
    }
}

Time Complexity: O(n) (optimal)
Space Complexity: O(1)
Master Memory Trick

Whenever the question contains these words:

Count
Number of
Total
Frequency
Occurrences

Your brain should immediately think:

Initialize count = 0
        ↓
Traverse
        ↓
Check condition
        ↓
count++
        ↓
Return count

I call this the CTCR Formula:

C → Counter (count = 0)
T → Traverse
C → Check the condition
R → Return the count
